rent Giving and Engagement Essential Resources Parent and Family Portal Tuition and Billing Financial Aid Contact Student Life How-Tos Find the Right Person or Office Connect with Faculty Expertise Participate in Campus Life Quick Links University Calendar Campus Directory Schools and Departments University News Essential Resources MyTU Workday Faculty Profiles Staff Directory University Policies How-Tos Application Tips Guide for Student Athletes Guide for International Applicants Quick Links Majors and Minors Campus Life Undergraduate Research Academic Success Essential Resources Apply to Trinity Cost and Financial Aid Visit Trinity Request Information How-Tos Plan Your Campus Visit Get to and Around Campus Make the Most of Your Time in San Antonio Quick Links Events Calendar Campus Map Things to Do in San Antonio Essential Resources Visit Trinity Directions and Parking Virtual Tour Connect with Faculty Expertise Home arrow_drop_down Home Connect with Faculty Expertise Explore Trinity’s academic programs, faculty profiles, teaching, research, creative work, and areas of expertise. In this Guide Trinity faculty are teachers, mentors, scholars, researchers, artists, and public experts. Use academic program pages and faculty profiles to learn who is working in a particular field and how their work connects with students and the wider community. Begin with an academic area Browse Trinity’s academic programs and departments when you want to understand a field of study, identify a department, or see how a subject is taught. ·         Explore majors, minors, programs, and departments. ·         Review department pages for faculty, courses, research, and related opportunities. ·         Use faculty profiles to learn about teaching and scholarly interests. Search for a person or topic The employee directory can help you locate faculty by name or department. Faculty spotlights and University news may provide additional context about current work. ·         Search the directory by department. ·         Review faculty profiles and linked publications or projects. ·         Search University news for a topic, faculty member, or area of research. Make contact When reaching out, explain who you are, the topic you are interested in, and why you believe the faculty member or department may be the right contact. ·         Keep the first message focused and specific. ·         For media requests, use the University’s designated communications contact when appropriate. ·         Contact the academic department when you are unsure which faculty member best matches the request. Start here Faculty Directory arrow_right_alt Employee Directory arrow_right_alt Academic Programs arrow_right_alt Faculty Spotlights arrow_right_alt 1 Trinity Place San Antonio, TX 78212 (210) 999-7011 Campus Directory News Athletics University Events University Calendars Library Maps and Directions Employment Courses of Study Bulletin Emergency Info Hire a Tiger The Trinity University Store MyTU Student Consumer Information Report an Incident University Policies Digital Accessibility © 2026 Trinity University. All rights reserved."
